WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:04.181
Guided updates require the restricted Linux host update service and matching

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.312
application mounts.

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:09.301
Install the checksummed host kit once during an idle maintenance window,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.646
then activate the matching application image.

00:00:11.857 --> 00:00:15.782
An enabled and active host service alone does not prove that the container

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:16.764
has been updated.

00:00:17.105 --> 00:00:20.945
Windows Docker Desktop retains its reviewed manual update procedure.

00:00:21.201 --> 00:00:23.810
The web application does not need the Docker socket.

00:00:24.165 --> 00:00:28.410
Open Appliance Operations, Updates, and Review Storage Before Upload.

00:00:28.645 --> 00:00:32.122
Check the capacity allowance and review eligible cleanup candidates.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:35.461
Remove only specifically reviewed obsolete artifacts.

00:00:35.791 --> 00:00:40.463
Keep the selected package, retained rollback material and protected backups.

00:00:40.741 --> 00:00:42.612
Nothing is automatically pruned.

00:00:42.906 --> 00:00:46.703
Storage review cannot approve an installation, and a fixed amount of free

00:00:46.788 --> 00:00:50.372
space is not a guarantee that backup and image expansion will fit.

00:00:50.799 --> 00:00:54.468
Obtain the complete trusted offline ZIP and verify its independently

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:55.693
published checksum.

00:00:55.937 --> 00:01:00.033
Upload and verify the ZIP, then select its imported package and check

00:01:00.118 --> 00:01:00.801
readiness.

00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:06.220
The service checks image identity, protocol, Compose and database access,

00:01:06.561 --> 00:01:08.169
storage and active work.

00:01:08.454 --> 00:01:11.931
Resolve every blocker and obtain a fresh readiness plan.

00:01:12.251 --> 00:01:16.006
Importing a package does not run its host installer or replace the running

00:01:16.134 --> 00:01:16.781
application.

00:01:17.306 --> 00:01:22.767
Review the version and interruption notice, then type the exact I N S T A L

00:01:22.853 --> 00:01:24.090
L phrase shown.

00:01:24.474 --> 00:01:28.101
The plan expires after fifteen minutes and is bound to that operation.

00:01:28.442 --> 00:01:30.586
Select Back Up and Install once.

00:01:30.937 --> 00:01:34.991
The guided service stops the application, verifies the backup pair and

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:38.617
recreates the application while PostgreSQL remains running.

00:01:39.001 --> 00:01:42.927
Reconnect after interruption and inspect the retained operation rather than

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:43.745
submitting again.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.324
Review the completed operation report and verify the exact running image,

00:01:48.623 --> 00:01:52.196
source commit, application health and database readiness.

00:01:52.654 --> 00:01:56.708
The general release label may still say version one point eight point five

00:01:56.793 --> 00:02:00.546
release candidate one; the build identity distinguishes patches.

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:05.964
Check saved configurations, credentials, pipelines, schedules and recovery

00:02:06.177 --> 00:02:08.204
profiles before resuming automation.

00:02:08.524 --> 00:02:11.602
Keep the receipts and download the sanitized operation report.

00:02:12.126 --> 00:02:15.966
If the console is reachable, the previous-image recovery control requires

00:02:16.009 --> 00:02:19.977
independent database compatibility confirmation and its exact rollback

00:02:20.062 --> 00:02:20.671
phrase.

00:02:21.024 --> 00:02:25.718
It restores the retained application image, not the database, data, host

00:02:25.931 --> 00:02:28.768
settings or changes made to Nutanix targets.

00:02:29.131 --> 00:02:32.471
Use authorized host recovery when the console is unavailable.

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:37.390
Connected discovery is metadata-only: unattended downloads and automatic

00:02:37.433 --> 00:02:39.385
installation are not enabled.
